{"data": [{"author_id": "32372834", "created_at": "2026-11-12T20:43:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120980712102695411"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/wjtLXB5HcT", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2120980712102695411/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120980708889927680", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/wjtLXB5HcT"}]}, "id": "2120980712102695411", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2751, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Years ago, Wendy Valencia Montoya touched a flower in the Amazon rainforest, startling in its warmth. Back then, researchers thought that heat-producing plants mainly wielded heat as a way to volatize scents that tempt pollinators. \n\n“I decided to challenge this view and ask a https://t.co/wjtLXB5HcT", "url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2120980712102695411"}, {"author_id": "860158302", "created_at": "2026-11-12T20:22:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120975422846296428"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Is self-enclosure life’s greatest trick? According to the lipid-first theory of the origin of life, a cell membrane gave primordial chemistry a place to gather.", "display_url": "quantamagazine.org/the-case-for-a…", "end": 198, "expanded_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/the-case-for-a-bubble-at-lifes-start-20261110/", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120172500231598080/JiyQOua9?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120172500231598080/JiyQOua9?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 175, "status": 200, "title": "The Case for a Bubble at Life’s Start | Quanta Magazine", "unwound_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/the-case-for-a-bubble-at-lifes-start-20261110/", "url": "https://t.co/U5h0rNkKBY"}]}, "id": "2120975422846296428", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1523, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Some scientists wonder if the repeated drying and refilling of ancient pools could have squeezed simple molecules between layers of lipids, thus beginning life as we know it. https://t.co/U5h0rNkKBY", "url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2120975422846296428"}, {"author_id": "860158302", "created_at": "2026-11-12T20:19:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120974667150172371"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Energetic pathways that make and break complex molecules are critical to all life. It’s even possible that these self-sustaining cycles could have been key at life’s beginning.", "display_url": "quantamagazine.org/what-is-the-me…", "end": 156, "expanded_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/what-is-the-metabolism-first-theory-for-the-origin-of-life-20261111/", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120535548368719873/PbcX3vJj?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120535548368719873/PbcX3vJj?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 133, "status": 200, "title": "What Is The Metabolism-First Theory for the Origin of Life? | Quanta Magazine", "unwound_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/what-is-the-metabolism-first-theory-for-the-origin-of-life-20261111/", "url": "https://t.co/dRAHQLN9Td"}]}, "id": "2120974667150172371", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1525, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "A team of researchers mimicked hydrothermal vents in their lab to model the chemical reactions that may have helped life first form.\nhttps://t.co/dRAHQLN9Td", "url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2120974667150172371"}, {"author_id": "28164923", "created_at": "2026-11-12T20:15:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120973666678690054"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "A once-modest company soared after ChatGPT unleashed demand for its chips.", "display_url": "on.wsj.com/4k8d2eD", "end": 60, "expanded_url": "https://on.wsj.com/4k8d2eD", "images": [{"height": 640, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120973669698502656/Pfntipyo?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120973669698502656/Pfntipyo?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 37, "status": 200, "title": "Nvidia’s Meteoric Rise, in One Chart", "unwound_url": "https://www.wsj.com/tech/nvidias-meteoric-rise-in-one-chart-2f47d54e?reflink=e2twmkts", "url": "https://t.co/OJ1Ydk4vSU"}]}, "id": "2120973666678690054", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 3672, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Nvidia’s Meteoric Rise, in One Chart https://t.co/OJ1Ydk4vSU", "url": "https://x.com/WSJmarkets/status/2120973666678690054"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-12T20:12:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120972912362426523"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "“On day one, governors should know kindergarten vaccination rates by county,” write Mandy Cohen and Ellen Montz.", "display_url": "bit.ly/4iRCjrc", "end": 257, "expanded_url": "https://bit.ly/4iRCjrc", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120813890053271553/IdYsLZ7w?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120813890053271553/IdYsLZ7w?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 234, "status": 200, "title": "3 things new governors must do to lead on health", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/12/new-governors-2027-health-priorities-agenda/", "url": "https://t.co/0TzJjuYKPW"}]}, "id": "2120972912362426523", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 963, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"To succeed in harnessing the power of state government to improve health and well-being and tackle affordability, new governors need to do three things: hire operators, see the trouble that’s already here, and set a focused agenda.\" https://t.co/0TzJjuYKPW", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2120972912362426523"}, {"author_id": "860158302", "created_at": "2026-11-12T19:58:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120969382629187662"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "RNA and peptides coevolving in the primordial world might have jointly served as a precursor to the modern ribosome.", "display_url": "quantamagazine.org/lifes-first-pe…", "end": 262, "expanded_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/lifes-first-peptides-may-have-grown-on-rna-20220524/", "images": [{"height": 292, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120969425826320384/VAE_6VMM?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 520}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120969425826320384/VAE_6VMM?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 239, "status": 200, "title": "Life’s First Peptides May Have Grown on RNA | Quanta Magazine", "unwound_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/lifes-first-peptides-may-have-grown-on-rna-20220524/", "url": "https://t.co/NoUV3KMJl7"}]}, "id": "2120969382629187662", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 1849, "like_count": 12, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "The protein-making process seen in cells today couldn’t have evolved in a harsh primordial world because it relies on proteins to protect the growing peptide chains. But what if the ancient way of growing peptides worked very differently? https://t.co/NoUV3KMJl7", "url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2120969382629187662"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-12T19:48:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120966910007234989"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "“Even as Kennedy and MAHA have cribbed from the Black activist playbook, they’ve actively undermined” Black Americans, writes Jerel Ezell.", "display_url": "statnews.com/2026/11/12/mah…", "end": 96, "expanded_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/12/maha-black-american-activists-voters-health-care-midterms/", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120827741972946946/iTkVDGT3?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120827741972946946/iTkVDGT3?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 73, "status": 200, "title": "I research MAHA and Black Americans. The relationship is complicated — and fascinating", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/12/maha-black-american-activists-voters-health-care-midterms/", "url": "https://t.co/zEIAoYOlzc"}]}, "id": "2120966910007234989", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1120, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"MAHA has co-opted issues that Black Americans have raised for decades.\" https://t.co/zEIAoYOlzc", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2120966910007234989"}, {"author_id": "14499829", "created_at": "2026-11-12T19:30:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120962392024617110"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/ydaeBQy0So", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/WHO/status/2120962392024617110/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120962389277282305", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/ydaeBQy0So"}]}, "id": "2120962392024617110", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 15857, "like_count": 18, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "Progress is being made in tackling tuberculosis (TB). But it's far too slow. \n\nThe TB incidence rate has fallen by just 14% since 2015, far short of the 50% reduction milestone for 2025. TB deaths have fallen by 35% over the same period, reaching the first mortality milestone in https://t.co/ydaeBQy0So", "url": "https://x.com/WHO/status/2120962392024617110"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-12T19:20:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120959966823567588"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Scores of doctors and scientists were elected last week. Will trust in science follow?", "display_url": "statnews.com/2026/11/12/tru…", "end": 216, "expanded_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/12/trust-in-science-physician-lawmakers-rebuild-belief/", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120841811073642496/d66w8c8T?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120841811073642496/d66w8c8T?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 193, "status": 200, "title": "Newly elected doctors and scientists hope to restore trust in science. It won't be easy", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/12/trust-in-science-physician-lawmakers-rebuild-belief/", "url": "https://t.co/uzaevvYlbH"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/qzZXlMxRjU", "end": 240, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2120959966823567588/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120959964223041536", "start": 217, "url": "https://t.co/qzZXlMxRjU"}]}, "id": "2120959966823567588", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1217, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "The midterm results clearly demonstrate that Americans remain deeply divided on core scientific issues, with some communities remaining distrustful of the cornerstones of public health policy. https://t.co/uzaevvYlbH https://t.co/qzZXlMxRjU", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2120959966823567588"}, {"author_id": "86626845", "created_at": "2026-11-12T19:20:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120959924171911488"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 56, "id": "32372834", "start": 40, "username": "ScienceMagazine"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/d6eagyKARO", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EricTopol/status/2120959924171911488/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120958457075671040", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/d6eagyKARO"}]}, "id": "2120959924171911488", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 13, "impression_count": 10895, "like_count": 43, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "Mapping a path to prevent breast cancer\n@ScienceMagazine \nDuctal carcinoma in situ (DCIS) is common and can be a precursor to invasive cancer. Elegant single cell and spatial omics work here tells us how DCIS progresses, earlier than previously anticipated, and lays a foundation https://t.co/d6eagyKARO", "url": "https://x.com/EricTopol/status/2120959924171911488"}, {"author_id": "15134240", "created_at": "2026-11-12T19:12:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120957817536258278"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/1geTQ4hkb3", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NIH/status/2120957817536258278/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120957814633820160", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/1geTQ4hkb3"}]}, "id": "2120957817536258278", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2622, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "The Muscular Dystrophy Coordinating Committee (MDCC) is seeking input on its renewed Action Plan which will serve as a blueprint to advance research and promote access to quality care and services for the entire muscular dystrophy community for the next decade.\n\nThe MDCC invites https://t.co/1geTQ4hkb3", "url": "https://x.com/NIH/status/2120957817536258278"}, {"author_id": "32372834", "created_at": "2026-11-12T19:05:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120956054389322168"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/OhFBC5u2c7", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2120956054389322168/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120956050522132480", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/OhFBC5u2c7"}]}, "id": "2120956054389322168", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 7864, "like_count": 16, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "Wild Asian elephants often form lasting social relationships, relying on one another for mutual care and support. However, these social groups are now at risk of unraveling owing to declining numbers.\n\nObservations conducted over more than a decade indicate that some endangered https://t.co/OhFBC5u2c7", "url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2120956054389322168"}, {"author_id": "32372834", "created_at": "2026-11-12T19:00:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120954849219031203"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 65, "start": 56, "tag": "melanoma"}], "mentions": [{"end": 217, "id": "137777298", "start": 207, "username": "scisignal"}], "urls": [{"description": "Blocking a Gq-coupled GPCR sensitizes uveal melanoma cells to an inhibitor of constitutively active G proteins.", "display_url": "scim.ag/3UqMaMB", "end": 241, "expanded_url": "https://scim.ag/3UqMaMB", "images": [{"height": 550, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120913032121307137/eAY-fL6C?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 715}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120913032121307137/eAY-fL6C?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 218, "status": 200, "title": "Gq-coupled GPCRs mediate the oncogenic activity of Gαq-Q209L/P mutants in uveal melanoma cells", "unwound_url": "https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/scisignal.aeg1191?utm_campaign=ScienceMagazine&utm_medium=ownedSocial&utm_source=twitter", "url": "https://t.co/oWuHiQO9Fr"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/nFYxJjMpCy", "end": 265, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2120954849219031203/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120954847105069056", "start": 242, "url": "https://t.co/nFYxJjMpCy"}]}, "id": "2120954849219031203", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 6388, "like_count": 20, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Examining G protein–coupled receptor signaling in uveal #melanoma cell lines, researchers have discovered a way to make these cells more sensitive to compounds that inhibit cancer-linked signaling pathways. @SciSignal https://t.co/oWuHiQO9Fr https://t.co/nFYxJjMpCy", "url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2120954849219031203"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-12T18:06:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120941214656577835"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "A massive scientific collaboration has produced the most detailed map yet of the basal ganglia, a key brain region involved in an array of psychiatric and neurologic disorders.", "display_url": "bit.ly/48hEy24", "end": 256, "expanded_url": "https://bit.ly/48hEy24", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120917246583115776/VpEO2rnX?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120917246583115776/VpEO2rnX?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 233, "status": 200, "title": "Scientists debut map of basal ganglia, a key brain region involved in an array of diseases", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/12/brain-map-basal-ganglia-offers-treatment-clues-parkinsons-schizophrenia/", "url": "https://t.co/mEAiuTOwHT"}]}, "id": "2120941214656577835", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1178, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "A massive scientific collaboration meant to unravel the mysteries of the human brain has produced the most detailed map yet of the basal ganglia, a region closely associated with a wide array of psychiatric and neurologic disorders. https://t.co/mEAiuTOwHT", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2120941214656577835"}, {"author_id": "28164923", "created_at": "2026-11-12T18:04:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120940818965913899"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "High earners in their early 60s can get up to $86,750 in these plans.", "display_url": "on.wsj.com/48P9NB